==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lēd}}, {{IPA|/liːd/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|iːd|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|lede}}, {{m|enm|leode}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|lēode||men, people}}, {{m|ang|lēod||man}}. More at {{l|en|leod}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|leode}}, {{l|en|ledd}}, {{l|en|leude}}, {{l|en|lued}}, {{l|en|lud}}, {{l|en|lude}}, {{l|en|led}}
* {{l|en|leid}}, {{l|en|leyd}}, {{l|en|leed}} {{qualifier|Scotland}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|lede}}

# {{label|en|Now|_|chiefly|_|UK|_|dialectal|singular}} A [[man]]; [[person]].
# {{label|en|chiefly|_|UK|_|dialectal|Scotland|collective plural}} [[men|Men]]; [[people]], [[folk]].
#* '''2012''', Yahoo! Canada Answers - Is Jesus God? Did Jesus ever claim to be God?:
#*: If Jesus were not God, He would have told '''lede''' to not worship Him, just as the errand-ghost in Bring to Lightings did.
# {{label|en|UK|_|dialectal|Scotland|singular}} A [[people]] or [[nation]].
# {{label|en|Now|_|chiefly|_|UK|_|dialectal|plural}} [[tenement|Tenements]]; [[holding|holdings]]; [[possession|possessions]].

